     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everybody;<div>i am newbie about R. I estimate in IRTPRO and R&#39;s MIRT package for a two-dimensional and dichotomous scoring test. </div><div>In R, all the a1 coefficients are negative. However, all of the IRTPRO&#39;s estimates are positive and their estimates are different. How can I resolve this situation?</div><div><br></div><div>I use mirt packaged via this code:</div><div><br></div><div>b23PLM=mirt(df,2, technical = list(NCYCLES=10000), itemtype = &quot;3PL&quot;, method = &#39;EM&#39;, SE=1)<br></div><div>coef(b23PLM)<br></div><div><br></div><div>Results for MIRT Package</div><div><div>$ï..M1</div><div>             a1     a2       d     g  u</div><div>par      -8.422  2.883 -12.581 0.173  1</div><div>CI_2.5  -13.028 -0.794 -19.349 0.155 NA</div><div>CI_97.5  -3.817  6.560  -5.813 0.192 NA</div><div><br></div><div>$M3</div><div>             a1     a2       d     g  u</div><div>par      -7.106  3.327 -13.336 0.189  1</div><div>CI_2.5  -12.287 -0.489 -22.744 0.172 NA</div><div>CI_97.5  -1.926  7.143  -3.928 0.208 NA</div><div><br></div><div>$M5</div><div>             a1     a2       d     g  u</div><div>par      -7.270  1.833  -8.137 0.247  1</div><div>CI_2.5  -10.506 -1.245 -12.108 0.219 NA</div><div>CI_97.5  -4.034  4.912  -4.165 0.278 NA</div><div><br></div><div>$M6</div><div>             a1     a2       d     g  u</div><div>par      -4.505 -1.577  -7.411 0.222  1</div><div>CI_2.5  -10.638 -5.013 -17.409 0.192 NA</div><div>CI_97.5   1.628  1.858   2.586 0.256 NA</div><div><br></div><div>$M7</div><div>            a1     a2      d     g  u</div><div>par     -3.336  1.046 -5.343 0.200  1</div><div>CI_2.5  -4.686 -0.383 -7.439 0.175 NA</div><div>CI_97.5 -1.985  2.475 -3.247 0.227 NA</div><div><br></div><div>$M8</div><div>            a1    a2      d     g  u</div><div>par     -2.418 1.471 -5.240 0.193  1</div><div>CI_2.5  -3.874 0.091 -8.042 0.166 NA</div><div>CI_97.5 -0.963 2.850 -2.439 0.224 NA</div><div><br></div><div>$M9</div><div>